# The mpv patch series, applied in this order by packaging/apply-series.sh.
# One file name per line. Every *.patch in this directory must be listed
# here, and each must apply exactly.
#
# 0001, 0002 and 0004 are upstreamable fixes: no zero MaxCLL/MaxFALL in the
# Wayland image description (Weston refuses it); the Profile 7
# enhancement-layer split without FFmpeg 9's dovi_split BSF (Ubuntu ships
# FFmpeg 8.1); and Wayland Vulkan swapchains that start pass-through, so the
# NVIDIA driver never holds the surface's one colour-management object.
# 0005 (upstreamable) lets an application give the OSC a film timeline
# (user-data/osc/film): plurx Player's live sessions show the whole film
# and hand seeks outside the stream back as "osc-film-seek". 0003 maps Dolby Vision with plurx's closed-form display
# management; it compiles against build-private.sh's copies of plurx's
# tools/dv_processing/dv_dm.h and dm_closed_form.h and the pinned libdovi
# header (packaging/libdovi/rpu_parser.h), in video/out/placebo/plurx/.
0001-wayland-don-t-send-an-unknown-MaxCLL-or-MaxFALL.patch
0002-demux-dovi_split-split-the-enhancement-layer-without.patch
0003-vo_gpu_next-map-Dolby-Vision-with-plurx-s-closed-for.patch
0004-vulkan-context-start-Wayland-swapchains-pass-through.patch
0005-osc-draw-a-film-timeline-the-application-provides.patch
